# Curated artefact -- Phase 3b, M2 run R4: QNX 8.0.0 on all six Cortex-A78AE cores of the Jetson Orin Nano (2026-09-10).
# Image m2-p6: startup-t234-orin-nano -vvv -P6 -Q disable -m992M -Wkeep -Dtcu, kimg sha256 prefix 5cae65e821edcdb9c2355310,
# entered by kexec from L4T R36.4.7. PART 1 was captured live over J14 (TCU, UART2_TXD pin 4), FT232R adapter, 115200 8N1, from
# Linux's kexec line to the first firmware lines after the reset. PART 2 is /sys/fs/pstore/console-ramoops-0 read on the next boot.
# RESULT: every M2 pass criterion held in this one run. Each secondary entered at EL2 through PSCI CPU_ON and printed its firmware
# EL2 registers before normalisation. 't234: cpu N up' appears for all six cores with the expected MPIDR, redistributor frame
# (frames 0-3 for cluster 0, 6 and 7 for cluster 1; frames 4 and 5 read without fault and hold the two absent cores' affinities),
# index and IPI routing value. All six parked in smp_spin, the kernel's gic_map and gicr_map carry the same six rows, pidin info
# lists six processors, and smpcheck printed 'SMPCHECK CENSUS PASS' and 'SMPCHECK RESULT PASS cpus=6/6 secs=60 reasons=none'.
# The image then warm-reset the board itself (PMC reset reason MAINSWRST) and L4T answered again 149 s after the launch.
# OBSERVED, NOT A CRITERION: both cluster-1 cores ran smpcheck's busy loop at about 12% of the cluster-0 rate, the same on both and
# in the previous run. The cause is not established; CPU frequency is uncontrolled in these runs.
# NOT SHOWN: anything under -Q enable (every core ran at EL1, no hypervisor host); that the kernel console callout is SMP-safe;
# direct IPI delivery; any timing figure; repeatability beyond this run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

